149 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The primary objective of this project is to design and develop a sophisticated Medical Retrieval-Augmented Generation \(RAG\) chatbot utilizing the BioMistral open-source Large Language Model \(LLM\). This chatbot will serve as an advanced tool for delivering accurate, contextually relevant, and reliable responses to user queries specifically focused on heart health. By integrating BioMistral LLM with a comprehensive heart health knowledge base stored in PDF format, the system will enable the retrieval of relevant, factual medical information to generate well-rounded and informative answers.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
150 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The project aims to create a platform that not only understands user queries but also draws on documented and validated medical resources to provide detailed, context-driven responses. This will enhance the accuracy and trustworthiness of the information, particularly in addressing key topics such as cardiovascular diseases, prevention strategies, treatments, and lifestyle recommendations. The chatbot will be designed to cater to a wide audience, from patients and caregivers to healthcare professionals, offering an accessible, user-friendly interface for gaining insights into heart health.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
151 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Through this project, the ultimate goal is to reduce the information gap in the field of cardiovascular health by creating an interactive tool that combines state-of-the-art AI technology with expert-validated knowledge. This chatbot will support better-informed decisions, promote heart health awareness, and empower users to take proactive steps in managing and improving their cardiovascular well-being. By making reliable medical information more accessible, the project seeks to contribute meaningfully to public health and healthcare education, fostering a deeper understanding of heart health issues.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
