/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Answer:  Atherosclerosis is a condition in which plaque builds up inside the arteries. This can reduce blood flow and may lead to heart attack, stroke or other health problems. It is caused by many factors including smoking, high cholesterol, high blood pressure, diabetes, obesity, lack of exercise, ageing and family history.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 22 0 R
